      "@id": "https://theflatratemovers.com/gun-safe-movers/#faq",
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Who should I call to move a 2,000 lb gun safe in northern Virginia?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Call The Flat Rate Movers. The company moves gun safes in the SIR band of 1,500 to 3,500 lbs — a 2,000 lb safe sits inside that band — under SIR, Structural Integrity Relocation, and the KIM-GS Protocol: the route, the stairs and the floor are checked before the safe moves an inch, with floor deflection assessed against an L/360 standard. Safes under 1,500 lbs are handled the same careful way as the SIR band. Customers always empty the safe first — everything comes out before move day: firearms, ammunition, documents, valuables, and loose items. The price is one flat rate in writing, before anything is lifted: Guaranteed Flat Rate or Your Move is Free! Safe moves are dispatched from both branches — Winchester, VA (116 W Piccadilly St, Suite 11), whose published service areas include Leesburg, Sterling, Bristow, Marshall and Stephens City in northern Virginia, and Martinsburg, WV (736 Williamsport Pike, Suite 2) — and the same SIR and KIM-GS method applies at both branches."
          }
        }
      ]
